{"content":[{"c":["HORN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Musical instrument frequently made from a ram’s horn. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MusicalInstruments_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MusicalInstruments_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MusicalInstruments_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Musical Instruments (Hatzotzrot)"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Figuratively, a symbol of power (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.22.11","r":"1Kgs.22.11","rawR":"1Kgs.22.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.22.11","value":"1Kgs.22.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 22:11"},") expressing dominance over the weak (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.34.21","r":"Ezek.34.21","rawR":"Ezek.34.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.34.21","value":"Ezek.34.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 34:21"},"), forces of destruction (",{"href":"?bref=Zech.1.18-21","r":"Zech.1.18-21","rawR":"Zech.1.18-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.1.18-21","value":"Zech.1.18-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zec 1:18-21"},"), and deliverance from oppression (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.22.11","r":"1Kgs.22.11","rawR":"1Kgs.22.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.22.11","value":"1Kgs.22.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 22:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.18.10","r":"2Chr.18.10","rawR":"2Chr.18.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.18.10","value":"2Chr.18.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 18:10"},"). Thus, the horn has two connotations: rescue and force (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.22.3","r":"2Sam.22.3","rawR":"2Sam.22.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.22.3","value":"2Sam.22.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 22:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.18.2","r":"Ps.18.2","rawR":"Ps.18.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.18.2","value":"Ps.18.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 18:2"},"). The sprouting of the horn referred to in ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.132.17","r":"Ps.132.17","rawR":"Ps.132.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.132.17","value":"Ps.132.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalm 132:17"}," could mean the continuation of the kingly line. ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.75.10","r":"Ps.75.10","rawR":"Ps.75.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.75.10","value":"Ps.75.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalm 75:10"}," declares that the horns of the wicked shall be cut off but those of the righteous exalted. The symbolic imagery in Daniel and Revelation reinforces the use of the horn to represent power and authority (",{"href":"?bref=Dan.7.1-8.27","r":"Dan.7.1-8.27","rawR":"Dan.7.1-8.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Dan.7.1-8.27","value":"Dan.7.1-8.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dn 7–8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.13.1-18","r":"Rev.13.1-18","rawR":"Rev.13.1-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.13.1-18","value":"Rev.13.1-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rv 13"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Rev.17.1-18","r":"Rev.17.1-18","rawR":"Rev.17.1-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.17.1-18","value":"Rev.17.1-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. A container. The ram’s horn, goat’s horn, and horn of a wild ox were used as containers for liquid. They were also ceremonial receptacles for oil (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.16.1,13","r":"1Sam.16.1,13","rawR":"1Sam.16.1,13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.16.1,13","value":"1Sam.16.1,13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 16:1, 13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.1.39","r":"1Kgs.1.39","rawR":"1Kgs.1.39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.1.39","value":"1Kgs.1.39"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 1:39"},"). Cows’ horns were forbidden for any religious or ceremonial use."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Four horn-shaped projections jutting from the four corners of the tabernacle and temple altars (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.27.2","r":"Exod.27.2","rawR":"Exod.27.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.27.2","value":"Exod.27.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 27:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.30.2-3","r":"Exod.30.2-3","rawR":"Exod.30.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.30.2-3","value":"Exod.30.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"30:2-3"},"). These altar horns were coated with sacrificial blood and denoted an area of sanctuary (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.29.12","r":"Exod.29.12","rawR":"Exod.29.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.29.12","value":"Exod.29.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 29:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.4.7,18","r":"Lev.4.7,18","rawR":"Lev.4.7,18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.4.7,18","value":"Lev.4.7,18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 4:7, 18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.1.50-51","r":"1Kgs.1.50-51","rawR":"1Kgs.1.50-51","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.1.50-51","value":"1Kgs.1.50-51"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 1:50-51"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Horn","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 22:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.22.11","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.22.11","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.22.11"},{"anchorText":"Ez 34:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.34.21","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.34.21","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.34.21"},{"anchorText":"Zec 1:18-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Zech.1.18-21","rawQueryValue":"Zech.1.18-21","sourceRefExact":"Zech.1.18-21"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 22:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.22.11","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.22.11","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.22.11"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 18:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.18.10","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.18.10","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.18.10"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 22:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.22.3","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.22.3","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.22.3"},{"anchorText":"Ps 18:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.18.2","rawQueryValue":"Ps.18.2","sourceRefExact":"Ps.18.2"},{"anchorText":"Psalm 132:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.132.17","rawQueryValue":"Ps.132.17","sourceRefExact":"Ps.132.17"},{"ancho